@startuml
!include style.puml
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 160

participant ":LoanHandler" as Handler
participant "LoanReturnStorage" as Store <<utility>>
participant "LoanStorage.FileSnapshot" as Snapshots <<class>>
participant ":EquipmentHandler" as Inventory
participant "LoanStorage" as Loans <<utility>>

Handler -> Store: save(...)
activate Store
loop each configured file
    Store -> Snapshots: capture(file)
    activate Snapshots
    create participant "snapshot:\nLoanStorage.FileSnapshot" as Snapshot
    Snapshots -> Snapshot: new(path, existed, regularFile, contents)
    Snapshot --> Snapshots: snapshot
    Snapshots --> Store: snapshot
    deactivate Snapshots
end
note right of Store
Capture equipment, loans and sequence paths.
Each loop iteration creates one FileSnapshot.
Keep path state and any regular-file bytes
before any writes begin.
end note
Store -> Inventory: saveReturnAssessment(...)
Inventory --> Store: equipment saved
Store -> Loans: save(...)
Loans --> Store: IOException (example: sequence save failed)
loop each snapshot
    Store -> Snapshot: restore()
    Snapshot --> Store: restored, or IOException retained
end
Store --> Handler: IOException with any restoration errors
deactivate Store
note over Handler
Wrap IOException as LoanReturnUnsuccessful;
no live assessment or returned flag is changed.
The caller reports a failed restoration when necessary.
Equipment-save failures use the same restoration loop.
end note
@enduml
